1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,503
This tutorial creates a new project and
adds its first property.

2
00:00:04,503 --> 00:00:08,596
As a Company Admin, open Leasing, then
Properties and Units.

3
00:00:08,596 --> 00:00:11,462
Each row is a project: one site,

4
00:00:11,462 --> 00:00:14,327
with its units, vacancies, occupancy, and
revenue.

5
00:00:14,327 --> 00:00:18,830
Before creating anything, search for the
name you plan to use.

6
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:22,514
Nothing matches Creek Gardens, so there is
no duplicate.

7
00:00:22,514 --> 00:00:24,561
Open More, then Add Project.

8
00:00:24,561 --> 00:00:27,836
A project groups the properties on one
site.

9
00:00:27,836 --> 00:00:32,748
Enter the English name, Oasis Crest Creek
Gardens, and the Arabic name.

10
00:00:32,748 --> 00:00:36,023
Choose the emirate, Dubai, and the type,
Residential.

11
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:39,298
Add the street address and the Makani
number,

12
00:00:39,298 --> 00:00:42,573
the ten-digit number that identifies the
building's entrance.

13
00:00:42,573 --> 00:00:47,485
Fixed expenses holds the site's yearly
running costs, such as service charges.

14
00:00:47,485 --> 00:00:48,304
Select Create.

15
00:00:48,304 --> 00:00:51,988
The project joins the list, with no units
yet.

16
00:00:51,988 --> 00:00:54,034
Now add its first property.

17
00:00:54,034 --> 00:00:55,263
Select Add Property.

18
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:59,356
Here, a property is one rentable unit
inside a project.

19
00:00:59,356 --> 00:01:02,222
Select the project, enter the unit number,

20
00:01:02,222 --> 00:01:05,087
CG-101, and choose the type, 2 BHK.

21
00:01:05,087 --> 00:01:07,543
Enter the size in square feet.

22
00:01:07,543 --> 00:01:09,181
New properties start Vacant.

23
00:01:09,181 --> 00:01:13,274
Enter the expected yearly rent, 98,000
dirhams, and select Create.

24
00:01:13,274 --> 00:01:16,958
The project's Units and Vacant columns now
count one.

25
00:01:16,958 --> 00:01:19,414
Select Manage to open the project.

26
00:01:19,414 --> 00:01:24,327
The header shows its name, type, address,
and Makani number, and the

27
00:01:24,327 --> 00:01:28,829
tabs hold its buildings, units, contracts,
amenities, parking, and ledger accounts.

28
00:01:28,829 --> 00:01:31,695
On Units, CG-101 is listed as a

29
00:01:31,695 --> 00:01:34,151
vacant 2 BHK at 98,000 dirhams.

30
00:01:34,151 --> 00:01:39,063
Back on the list, Cards shows each project
as a card with

31
00:01:39,063 --> 00:01:43,566
its units, vacancies, occupancy, and
revenue, which is quick to scan.

32
00:01:43,566 --> 00:01:46,841
Table lines the projects up in columns,
which

33
00:01:46,841 --> 00:01:49,706
is better for comparing a larger
portfolio.

34
00:01:49,706 --> 00:01:52,981
The new project is ready for buildings,
contacts,

35
00:01:52,981 --> 00:01:56,256
amenities, and parking, which the next
tutorial adds.
